div.p:
Adopting the principles laid down by the acting President of the Council, M.
                    Briand, in his declaration of December 10th [9th],
                        1931;

Affirming that it is contrary to the spirit of the Covenant that the settlement
                    of the Sino-Japanese dispute should be sought under the stress of military
                    pressure on the part of either Party;

In view of the request formulated on February 12th by the Chinese Government that the dispute should be referred to the Assembly
                    in conformity with Article 15, paragraph 9, of the Covenant and in view of the
                    Council’s decision of February 19th;
